 ## Overview
-Weather & Cloud Parameterization defines the physical and visual properties for volumetric cloud rendering, controlling coverage, density, type, geometry, lighting, and noise interaction [S1, S2, unofficial]. It serves as the bridge between high-level scene design (e.g., "stratocumulus at 2000m") and the low-level volumetric representation [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Volumetric Cloud Raymarching](1248-volumetric-cloud-raymarching.md) by providing the structured data interface that drives those processes rather than handling the integration step, and from [Procedural Volume Cloud Modeling](2256-procedural-volume-cloud-modeling.md) which focuses on the noise generation algorithm [S1, S2, unofficial].
