 ## Background
-The methodology originates from real-time rendering techniques for volumetric clouds in games and simulations, specifically those utilizing procedural noise and ray marching [S1, S2, S4, unofficial]. The parameterization structures (such as `CloudConfig` and `VolumeParameters`) are derived from engine-specific implementations designed to balance visual fidelity with performance constraints like resolution scaling and temporal reprojection [S1, S2, unofficial]. The physical shading model incorporates approximations of multiple scattering and the Henyey-Greenstein phase function to simulate light transport within participating media [S3, unofficial].
